SABERES FRANÇA-BRASIL 2026 · PESQUISAS EM DIÁLOGO
Between Representation and Authentication
Female allegory and legal authority in the France–Brazil circulation, 1822–1906
Ana Vanzin
PhD candidate, PPGD/UFSC · Ius Gentium research group
Florianópolis, 13 November 2026
[Before starting: about 15 minutes. Plan B cuts are marked on each slide.] Good afternoon. Thank you to Ius Commune, to the Centre d’Histoire Judiciaire of Lille, and to our colleagues from Ghent and Trento. The title of this talk names two verbs that the legal order tends to keep together and that I would like to pull apart for fifteen minutes: to represent and to authenticate. The woman you see here is French. She was cast in Paris, at the Val d’Osne foundry, in the nineteenth century, and she lives about ten minutes from this auditorium, at the foot of the main staircase of the Palácio Cruz e Sousa.
