ZWISCHENRAUM, 1494–1603
The less the figure tells a story, the more it fixes a norm.
The blindfold that blinds Justice also blinds the allegory to its own exclusion: the woman who personifies the forum is the one barred from it.
[5:45–6:30] Between 1494 and 1603, in this Zwischenraum, the female figure passes from a character in a narrative to an emblem of authority. The less the figure tells a story, the more it fixes a norm. And for a legal audience, one sentence to keep: the blindfold that blinds Justice also blinds the allegory to its own exclusion. The woman who personifies the forum is the woman barred from it.
