DECEMBER 1890
One month ties image, value and law
6 Dec
Decree 1.127
The Penal Code of 1890 enters into force in the Federal District on 20 Dec 1890; in Minas Gerais and the coastal states, on 1 Feb 1891.
7 Dec
Decree 1.154, art. 3º
Authorises the fusion that creates the Banco da República. Notes issue “na razão do triplo do deposito em ouro”: three times the gold deposit.
30 Dec
Decree 1.227, art. 10 and § 11
Its statutes admit “moedas de ouro nacionaes, inglezas (soberanos e meios soberanos), e francezas de 20 e 10 francos” in the metallic base; forged notes carry the penalties of moeda falsa.
French gold circulates in Brazil with legal tender, by the text of a Brazilian decree.
Local nuance: in Santa Catarina, counterfeit coin was still punished by the Criminal Code of 1830 until February 1891.
Ana Vanzin · Between Representation and Authentication
9
[9:00–10:30] December 1890 is the month in which the Republic ties together image, value and law. 6 December, Decree 1.127: the Penal Code of 1890 comes into force in the Federal District on 20 December; in the coastal states, from Rio Grande do Sul to Pará, and in Minas Gerais, on 1 February 1891. A local nuance: here in Santa Catarina, counterfeit coin was still punished under the Criminal Code of 1830 until February 1891. 7 December, Decree 1.154: it creates the Banco da República and regulates issue; the explanatory statement is Ruy Barbosa’s. Article 3º fixes issue at three times the gold deposit. 30 December, Decree 1.227 approves the bank’s statutes: article 10 admits in the metallic base national gold coins, English sovereigns and half-sovereigns, and French coins of 20 and 10 francs. French gold circulates in Brazil with legal tender, by the text of the statute. Its paragraph 11: “A falsificação de notas e a introdução de falsificadas serão punidas com as penas comminadas, pelo direito vigente, ao crime de moeda falsa.” [My translation: the forging of notes and the introduction of forged ones shall be punished with the penalties set, by the law in force, for the crime of counterfeit coin.] [If 10 minutes: one sentence for 1.127; mention 1.227 without § 11.]
